      "output": "**Water (H₂O)** is a simple yet remarkably versatile chemical compound that is essential for life and plays a central role in Earth’s physical and biological systems. Here’s a concise overview:\n\n| Aspect | Details |\n|--------|---------|\n| **Chemical Formula** | H₂O – two hydrogen atoms covalently bonded to one oxygen atom. |\n| **Molecular Structure** | Bent shape (≈104.5° bond angle) giving it a polar character. |\n| **States of Matter** | Solid (ice), liquid (water), gas (vapor). Transitions occur at 0 °C (freezing) and 100 °C (boiling) under standard atmospheric pressure. |\n| **Key Physical Properties** | • **High specific heat** – absorbs a lot of heat before temperature rises, moderating climates. <br>• **High surface tension** – allows insects to walk on it and creates droplets. <br>• **Excellent solvent** – dissolves many substances, enabling biochemical reactions. <br>• **Transparency** – allows light penetration, supporting aquatic life. |\n| **Biological Importance** | • **Solvent for cells** – transports nutrients, waste, and signals. <br>• **Regulates temperature** – through sweating, respiration, and circulation. <br>• **Structural component** – part of cell walls, connective tissues, and the cytoskeleton. |\n| **Geological & Environmental Role** | • **Hydrologic cycle** – evaporation, condensation, precipitation, runoff. <br>• **Erosion & weathering** – shapes landscapes. <br>• **Climate regulator** – stores and transports heat globally. |\n| **Human Uses** | • **Drinking & sanitation** – essential for health. <br>• **Industrial processes** – cooling, cleaning, chemical synthesis. <br>• **Agriculture** – irrigation. <br>• **Energy** – steam turbines, hydroelectric power. |\n| **Unique Features** | • **Density anomaly** – ice is less dense than liquid water, allowing it to float and insulate aquatic life in winter. <br>• **High cohesion & adhesion** – enables capillary action, crucial for plant water transport. |\n\nIn short, water is a polar, tri‑atomic molecule that exists naturally in all three states of matter, possesses unique physical properties that make it an excellent solvent, and is indispensable for life, climate regulation, and countless human activities."
